  <RESPONSE>
    The exit code 137 in a Docker container indicates that the process was terminated by the operating system using a `SIGKILL` signal.
    
    In Docker, this most commonly happens when the container exceeds its allocated memory limit, triggering the Out Of Memory (OOM) Killer. The exit code is calculated as $128 + \text{signal number}$. Since `SIGKILL` has a signal number of 9, the resulting exit code is $128 + 9 = 137$.
    
    Final Answer: The exit code 137 indicates that the container was terminated by a `SIGKILL` signal, most commonly due to an Out Of Memory (OOM) event.
    
